{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-32772" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 6 & -4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ \\boxed{} & \\boxed{} & \\boxed{} \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}.\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. From left to right, what are the missing elements from the second row of the matrix $U?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-32772" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $U$ in the LU decomposition is obtained from the original matrix $A$ by row-reducing using Gaussian elementation. In particular, to make $0$ at the position ${a}_{21}$ of the matrix $A,$ we proceed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 6 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 6 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the elements from the second row of $U$ are $0,-5,$ and $4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-32772" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a4772949fd9d4d2feff087b1e5e191bd56a55f219038497a2706266f679202f"} {"question" "q-32772" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-32772" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0,\\,-2,\\,3"] ["math" "0,\\,-2,\\,4"] ["math" "0,\\,-5,\\,1"] ["math" "0,\\,-5,\\,3"] ["math" "0,\\,-5,\\,4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-32772" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0,\\,-5,\\,4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-106963" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 7 & 18 & -19\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 9 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\boxed{}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}.\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. What is the value of ${u}_{33}$ in the matrix $U?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-106963" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $U$ in the LU decomposition is obtained from the original matrix $A$ by row-reducing using Gaussian elementation. In particular, to make zeros below the main diagonal, we proceed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 7 & 18 & -19\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 18 & -19\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-7){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 18 & -26\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-9){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${u}_{33}=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-106963" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a4772949fd9d4d2feff087b1e5e191bd56a55f219038497a2706266f679202f"} {"question" "q-106963" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-106963" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-13"] ["math" "-26"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-106963" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-106960" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 7 & 9 \\\\ 40 & -13 & 8\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 0 \\\\ \\boxed{} & \\boxed{} & \\boxed{} \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}.\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. From left to right, what are the missing elements from the second row of the matrix $U?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-106960" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $U$ in the LU decomposition is obtained from the original matrix $A$ by row-reducing using Gaussian elementation. In particular, to make $0$ at the position ${a}_{21}$ of the matrix $A,$ we proceed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 7 & 9 \\\\ 40 & -13 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 40 & -13 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the elements from the second row of $U$ are $0,3,$ and $9.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-106960" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a4772949fd9d4d2feff087b1e5e191bd56a55f219038497a2706266f679202f"} {"question" "q-106960" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-106960" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0,\\,11,\\,9"] ["math" "0,\\,3,\\,2"] ["math" "0,\\,3,\\,9"] ["math" "0,\\,5,\\,2"] ["math" "0,\\,5,\\,9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-106960" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0,\\,3,\\,9"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-105526" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}3 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}3 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -10 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\boxed{}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}.\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. What is the value of ${u}_{33}$ in the matrix $U?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-105526" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $U$ in the LU decomposition is obtained from the original matrix $A$ by row-reducing using Gaussian elementation. In particular, to make zeros below the main diagonal, we proceed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -10 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -10 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${u}_{33}=-3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-105526" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a4772949fd9d4d2feff087b1e5e191bd56a55f219038497a2706266f679202f"} {"question" "q-105526" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-105526" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3"] ["math" "-7"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-105526" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-106959" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 63 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 9 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & -1 \\\\ \\boxed{} & \\boxed{} & \\boxed{} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}.\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. From left to right, what are the missing elements from the second row of the matrix $U?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-106959" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $U$ in the LU decomposition is obtained from the original matrix $A$ by row-reducing using Gaussian elementation. In particular, to make $0$ at the position ${a}_{21}$ of the matrix $A,$ we proceed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 63 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 63 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the elements from the second row of $U$ are $0,3,$ and $-4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-106959" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a4772949fd9d4d2feff087b1e5e191bd56a55f219038497a2706266f679202f"} {"question" "q-106959" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-106959" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0,\\,-3,\\,4"] ["math" "0,\\,-4,\\,-5"] ["math" "0,\\,-4,\\,3"] ["math" "0,\\,3,\\,-4"] ["math" "0,\\,3,\\,-6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-106959" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0,\\,3,\\,-4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-106968" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -12 & -8 & -4 \\\\ 36 & -32 & 46\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 9 & \\boxed{} & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. What is the value of the entry ${l}_{32}$ in the matrix $L?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-106968" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $U$ in the LU decomposition is obtained from the original matrix $A$ by row-reducing using Gaussian elementation. In particular, to make zeros below the main diagonal, we proceed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -12 & -8 & -4 \\\\ 36 & -32 & 46\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 5 \\\\ 36 & -32 & 46\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-9){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -32 & 19\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we want to make $0$ at the position ${a}_{32}$ using Gaussian elimination. To do this, we take the $3$rd row of $A,$ and we add the $2$nd row of $A$ multiplied by $-4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -32 & 19\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe entry ${l}_{32}$ of the matrix $L$ is the factor next to ${R}_{2},$ taken with the opposite sign:\n\n$$\n{l}_{32}=-(-4)=4.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-106968" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a4772949fd9d4d2feff087b1e5e191bd56a55f219038497a2706266f679202f"} {"question" "q-106968" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-106968" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-106968" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-32726" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\boxed{} & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. What is the value of the entry ${l}_{31}$ in the matrix $L?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-32726" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We want to make $0$ at the position ${a}_{31}$ using Gaussian elimination. To do this, we take the $3$rd row of $A,$ and we add the $1$st row of $A$ multiplied by $-2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe entry ${l}_{31}$ of the matrix $L$ is the factor next to ${R}_{1},$ taken with the opposite sign:\n\n$$\n{l}_{31}=-(-2)=2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-32726" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a4772949fd9d4d2feff087b1e5e191bd56a55f219038497a2706266f679202f"} {"question" "q-32726" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-32726" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-32726" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-105599" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}4 & -6 & 7 \\\\ -8 & 10 & -10 \\\\ 4 & 6 & -9\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & \\boxed{} & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}4 & -6 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. What is the value of the entry ${l}_{32}$ in the matrix $L?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-105599" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $U$ in the LU decomposition is obtained from the original matrix $A$ by row-reducing using Gaussian elementation. In particular, to make zeros below the main diagonal, we proceed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -6 & 7 \\\\ -8 & 10 & -10 \\\\ 4 & 6 & -9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & -6 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 6 & -9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & -6 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 12 & -16\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we want to make $0$ at the position ${a}_{32}$ using Gaussian elimination. To do this, we take the $3$rd row of $A,$ and we add the $2$nd row of $A$ multiplied by $6:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}4 & -6 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 12 & -16\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+6{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & -6 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe entry ${l}_{32}$ of the matrix $L$ is the factor next to ${R}_{2},$ taken with the opposite sign:\n\n$$\n{l}_{32}=-(6)=-6.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-105599" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a4772949fd9d4d2feff087b1e5e191bd56a55f219038497a2706266f679202f"} {"question" "q-105599" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-105599" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-105599" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-105601" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -4 & 7\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & \\boxed{} & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. What is the value of the entry ${l}_{32}$ in the matrix $L?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-105601" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $U$ in the LU decomposition is obtained from the original matrix $A$ by row-reducing using Gaussian elementation. In particular, to make zeros below the main diagonal, we proceed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -4 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+1{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -4 \\\\ 8 & -4 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -18 & 17\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we want to make $0$ at the position ${a}_{32}$ using Gaussian elimination. To do this, we take the $3$rd row of $A,$ and we add the $2$nd row of $A$ multiplied by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -18 & 17\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe entry ${l}_{32}$ of the matrix $L$ is the factor next to ${R}_{2},$ taken with the opposite sign:\n\n$$\n{l}_{32}=-(2)=-2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-105601" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a4772949fd9d4d2feff087b1e5e191bd56a55f219038497a2706266f679202f"} {"question" "q-105601" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-105601" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-105601" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-106966" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 18 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\boxed{} & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. What is the value of the entry ${l}_{31}$ in the matrix $L?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-106966" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We want to make $0$ at the position ${a}_{31}$ using Gaussian elimination. To do this, we take the $3$rd row of $A,$ and we add the $1$st row of $A$ multiplied by $-1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 18 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 18 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe entry ${l}_{31}$ of the matrix $L$ is the factor next to ${R}_{1},$ taken with the opposite sign:\n\n$$\n{l}_{31}=-(-1)=1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-106966" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a4772949fd9d4d2feff087b1e5e191bd56a55f219038497a2706266f679202f"} {"question" "q-106966" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-106966" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-106966" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-32749" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ -9 & -6 & -6 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $D=LU$ is the LU decomposition of the matrix $D$ given above, what is the value of ${l}_{32}\\cdot {u}_{23}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-32749" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's apply our standard LU factorization algorithm.\n\nWe reduce the matrix $D$ to row echelon form to obtain the matrix $U,$ as usual. However, instead of writing zeros below the main diagonal, we will instead write down the entries of the matrix $L.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ -9 & -6 & -6 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 6 & 9 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+1{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 6 & 9 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{3}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 6 & 9 \\\\ -1 & \\,\\frac{1}{3}\\, & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,U=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${l}_{32}=\\frac{1}{3}$ and ${u}_{23}=9,$ we get\n\n$$\n{l}_{32}\\cdot {u}_{23}=\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 9=3.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062864/state.json" "file_sha256" "667df05684778eae9ede43c40bf38ff4d3afd2d183b1d27950a4b5c6a2fc3ff5"} {"question" "q-32749" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14